{
	"info": {
		"_postman_id": "a1b2c3d4-e5f6-7890-abcd-ef1234567890",
		"name": "OpenMind Saga Orchestrator",
		"description": "Postman collection for testing the OpenMind Saga Orchestrator microservices (Java/Spring Boot port).\n\n## Services\n- **Orchestrator** (Port 5000): Axon-managed saga that coordinates the order placement workflow\n- **Order** (Port 5001): Manages order creation and storage\n- **Payment** (Port 5002): Handles payment processing (simulated gateway) + manual retry\n- **Fulfillment** (Port 5003): Manages order fulfillment and shipping (simulated warehouse)\n- **Email** (Port 5004): Sends notification emails (simulated, stateless)\n\n## Workflow\n1. First create an order using \"Create Order\" in the Order Service\n2. Then use \"Place Order (Start Saga)\" to initiate the placement process\n3. Poll \"Get Saga State\" to watch the saga move through states (it's removed from the store once it ends, so a 404 there means it already completed/cancelled)\n4. Check \"Get Order\" / \"Get Payment\" / \"Get Fulfillment\" for each service's own view\n5. If the saga parks in `PaymentNotPaid`, use Payment Service's \"Retry Payment\" to unblock it",
		"schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
	},
